      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9d055842-9456-5dd4-8722-44e5043cee53",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: The Boarding House, San Francisco, California\n- People: David Allen, Robin Williams, Steve Martin, Tom Waits, Dolly Parton, Patti Smith, Neil Young, Bette Midler, Billy Joel, Bob Marley, Mason Williams, Randy Newman, Jim Croce, Harry Chapin\n- Groups: The Tubes, Talking Heads, Old and in the Way, Dan Hicks & His Hot Licks\n- Products: Let's Get Small, A Wild and Crazy Guy, Comedy Is Not Pretty\n- Topics: music clubs, comedy clubs, live recordings\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Waits was born on December 7, 1949, and he is an American singer-songwriter, composer, and actor.\n- The Boarding House was a music and comedy nightclub at 960 Bush Street in San Francisco, California.\n- David Allen opened The Boarding House in 1971.\n- Robin Williams launched his career at The Boarding House.\n- Steve Martin's first three albums, \"Let's Get Small,\" \"A Wild and Crazy Guy,\" and \"Comedy Is Not Pretty,\" were recorded there in whole or in part.\n- The Boarding House hosted musical acts including Dolly Parton, Patti Smith, Neil Young, Bette Midler, Billy Joel, Bob Marley, Mason Williams, The Tubes, Talking Heads, Old and in the Way, Randy Newman, Dan Hicks & His Hot Licks, Jim Croce, Harry Chapin, and Tom Waits.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a2d4e276-c94b-5c0c-857e-cfc78037b54c",
        "text": "Page: The Boarding House (nightclub). Sentence: The Boarding House was a music and comedy nightclub located at 960 Bush Street in San Francisco, California, opened by David Allen in 1971.\nPage: The Boarding House (nightclub). Sentence: Robin Williams launched his career there and Steve Martin's first three albums, \"Let's Get Small\", \"A Wild and Crazy Guy\", and \"Comedy Is Not Pretty\" were recorded there, in whole or in part.\nPage: The Boarding House (nightclub). Sentence: The club was also host to a multitude of musical acts, such as Dolly Parton, Patti Smith, Neil Young, Bette Midler, Billy Joel, Bob Marley, Mason Williams, The Tubes, Talking Heads, Old and in the Way, Randy Newman, Dan Hicks & His Hot Licks, Jim Croce, Harry Chapin and Tom Waits.\nPage: Tom Waits. Sentence: Thomas Alan \"Tom\" Waits (born December 7, 1949) is an American singer-songwriter, composer, and actor.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
